Welcome to the README file for the folder dedicated to the PCA-based FFNN models.

Using PCA to compress the gene bulk dataset, we train and test FFNN models adapted to the PCA input.
The output will be the transcript expression in the normal dimensions. 

(!) If you haven't already, be sure to read the README file in the main DeepIsoQ folder. 
Furthermore, be sure that you have set up a proper virtual environment (venv) and that you have run the preprocessing script, etc. 

Remark about Python scripts: Be sure to update some of the corresponding content of the job scripts if you plan on running the scripts. I.e., ensure that the venv name of the job script and the venv that you are using match. 


OVERVIEW OF THE FILES:

1) Notebook 
This compiles the code of all the scripts. It will give a more coherent explanation and walk-through of all the code in the different scripts. 

2) pca_script.py
This is the original FFNN model, which was initially trained for the PCA data. It doesn't have any hyperparameter optimization, and the hyperparameters were chosen arbitrarily. 

3) pca_dim_search.py
This script keeps the hyperparameters fixed but tries out various different amounts of PCA components, to test to what degree the dimensionality reduction affects the performance, in order to approximate which PCA component will be the best one for all the models. (Note: It was 1000 PCA components).
This script produces the plot, which can be found in

4) multiple_pca_script.py
Similar to the 'ffnn_search/ffnn_search_v2.py' script. It uses a randomization approach to explore the best hyperparameter setting. 

5) pca_best_model.py
This script trains and tests the best model, which was found by the 'multiple_pca_script.py' script. It also produces the final script and metrics, which were stated in the report. 


